{"type":"TEXT","ticket":429,"id":"ie427"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":427,"x":100,"y":1410,"rotation":0,"value":"ES8311 Rev 5.0 recommended supply: DVDD/PVDD 1.6-3.6 V, AVDD 1.7-3.6 V, absolute max 3.6 V; hold +3V3_SYS inside 3.0-3.6 V or the codec keeps no headroom.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":430,"id":"ie428"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":428,"x":100,"y":1430,"rotation":0,"value":"ES8311 Rev 5.0 documents no mic bias or electret supply pin; the MIC1N reference and the mic bias network stay TBD with the microphone selection.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":431,"id":"ie429"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":429,"x":100,"y":1450,"rotation":0,"value":"Codec I2C address is 0011 00x, CE strapped low gives 0x18; no clash with BMI270 0x68, RV-3028-C7 0x51/0x52, MAX17048 0x36 or DRV2605L 0x5A.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":432,"id":"ie430"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":430,"x":100,"y":1470,"rotation":0,"value":"ES8311 in slave mode expects externally supplied SCLK/LRCK; in master mode both derive from MCLK. Clock direction and ESP32 I2S feasibility remain unvalidated.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":433,"id":"ie431"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":431,"x":100,"y":1490,"rotation":0,"value":"PAM8302A delivers 0.72 W min / 0.80 W typ into 8 ohm at VDD=3.6 V and 10% THD+N; 1 W from a 3.3 V rail is not achievable. A 1 W speaker rating is not delivered power.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":434,"id":"ie432"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":432,"x":100,"y":1510,"rotation":0,"value":"Amp VDD drafted on VBAT (2.0-5.5 V allowed, SHDN must stay within VDD+0.3 V); +3V3_SYS and SYS stay open options - confirm cell impedance and peak current with the pack data.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":435,"id":"ie433"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":433,"x":100,"y":1530,"rotation":0,"value":"SHDN releases through R601/C614 for a datasheet 1-100 ms delay after VBAT rises; no spare GPIO exists for explicit enable control.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":436,"id":"ie434"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":434,"x":100,"y":1550,"rotation":0,"value":"One 220 nF cap per side merges the ES8311 output coupling with the PAM8302A CI 0.1-0.22 uF requirement; corner against the internal 10 k is about 72 Hz.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":437,"id":"ie435"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":435,"x":100,"y":1570,"rotation":0,"value":"Filterless BTL: never reference SPK_P or SPK_N to ground, keep the pair short, and add the datasheet ferrite-bead filter when the runs exceed 20 cm.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":438,"id":"ie436"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":436,"x":100,"y":1590,"rotation":0,"value":"ES8311 typical circuit separates GND(SYS) from AGND with 0 ohm; one GND net is kept until the PCB ground-strategy decision is taken.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":439,"id":"ie437"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":437,"x":100,"y":1610,"rotation":0,"value":"Footprints, the ES8311 QFN-20 land pattern and the acoustic assembly are still not released.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":440,"id":"ie438"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":438,"x":1000,"y":1410,"rotation":0,"value":"ES8311 Rev 5.0 package drawing shows an unnumbered exposed die-attach pad and the typical circuit labels that pad 21/PGND, while the pin table lists only 1-20; U9 keeps 20 pins until the vendor release confirms the pad and its net.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
{"type":"TEXT","ticket":441,"id":"ie439"}||{"partId":"","groupId":"","locked":false,"zIndex":439,"x":1000,"y":1430,"rotation":0,"value":"PAM8302A gain is fixed by the internal 150k/10k pair at 23.5 dB. The ES8311 full-scale output is 0.4535 Vrms, so the amp clips before full codec volume; trim with the DAC volume register or add an external RIN of about 16k ohm once the acoustic target is set.","color":null,"fillColor":null,"fontFamily":null,"fontSize":5.51181,"strikeout":false,"underline":false,"italic":false,"fontWeight":false,"align":"LEFT_MIDDLE"}|
